<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ lab.lab_abbrev }} Clinical Genomics Report — {{ rep.accession }}</title>
<style>
  :root{--navy:#16305e;--navy2:#0f2447;--gold:#c9a24b;--gold-lt:#e3c987;--ink:#1c2530;
        --muted:#5b6470;--line:#d8dde4;--soft:#f4f7fb;--soft2:#eef3f9;}
  @page{size:A4;margin:12mm 14mm 15mm 14mm;}
  *{box-sizing:border-box;-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;}
  body{font:11px/1.5 Arial,Helvetica,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:var(--ink);margin:0;}
  h2{margin:0;color:var(--navy);}
  .wrap{max-width:182mm;margin:0 auto;}
  /* Repeating letterhead: a <thead> is repainted at the top of every printed page by Chrome,
     and (unlike position:fixed here) it reserves its own space so content never overlaps it. */
  .pagetbl{width:100%;max-width:182mm;margin:0 auto;border-collapse:collapse;}
  .pagetbl>thead{display:table-header-group;}
  .pagetbl>thead>tr>td,.pagetbl>tbody>tr>td{border:0;padding:0;background:transparent;}
  .headerband{padding-bottom:2.5mm;}
  .banner{display:block;margin:0 auto 3px;width:auto;max-width:100%;max-height:14mm;}
  .rule{height:3px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--navy) 62%,var(--gold) 62%);border-radius:2px;margin:4px 0 6px;}
  .lablogo{height:36px;display:block;}
  .doctype{text-align:right;} .doctype .t{font-size:15px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);}
  .doctype .s{font-size:9px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.4px;}
  .headrow{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-end;}
  .meta{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:2px 18px;background:var(--soft);
        border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:9px 12px;margin:8px 0 10px;font-size:10px;}
  .meta b{color:var(--navy);} .meta .k{color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.8px;}
  h2.sec{font-size:11.5px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold);padding-bottom:3px;margin:12px 0 6px;}
  table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:10px;margin:4px 0;}
  th,td{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:4px 7px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;}
  th{background:var(--soft2);color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;}
  .result{border:1px solid var(--navy);border-left:6px solid var(--navy);border-radius:6px;background:var(--soft);padding:10px 14px;margin:6px 0 4px;}
  .result .lead{font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);}
  /* ACMG classification colour convention (benign -> pathogenic heat scale) */
  .badge{display:inline-block;color:#fff;font-weight:700;font-size:9px;padding:2px 10px;border-radius:11px;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-left:6px;vertical-align:middle;}
  .badge.P{background:#b02a37;}                                   /* Pathogenic — red */
  .badge.LP{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#f76707 0%,#d6252f 100%);} /* Likely pathogenic — orange -> red */
  .badge.VUS{background:#e6a817;color:#3a2c07;}                   /* Uncertain significance — amber */
  .badge.LB{background:#66a80f;}                                  /* Likely benign — light green */
  .badge.B{background:#2f9e44;}                                   /* Benign — green */
  .legend{margin:6px 0 2px;font-size:8.5px;color:var(--muted);}
  .chip{display:inline-block;color:#fff;font-weight:600;font-size:8px;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:9px;margin:0 2px;}
  .chip.P{background:#b02a37;} .chip.LP{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#f76707,#d6252f);}
  .chip.VUS{background:#e6a817;color:#3a2c07;} .chip.LB{background:#66a80f;} .chip.B{background:#2f9e44;}
  .mono{font-family:"SF Mono",Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:9.5px;}
  ul{margin:4px 0 4px 16px;padding:0;} li{margin:2px 0;}
  .muted{color:var(--muted);} .small{font-size:9px;}
  .sign{margin-top:14px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:30px;}
  .sig{flex:1;} .sigline{border-bottom:1.3px solid var(--navy);height:26px;margin-bottom:3px;}
  .sig .role b{color:var(--navy);}
  .foot{margin-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:6px;font-size:8px;color:var(--muted);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;}
  .pagebreak{page-break-before:always;}
</style></head><body>
<table class="pagetbl">
<thead><tr><td>
  <div class="headerband">
    <img class="banner" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ lab.banner_b64 }}" alt="{{ lab.institute }}"/>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <div class="headrow">
      <img class="lablogo" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ lab.lab_logo_b64 }}" alt="{{ lab.lab_name }}"/>
      <div class="doctype"><div class="t">Clinical Genomics Report</div><div class="s">{{ rep.report_type }}</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</td></tr></thead>
<tbody><tr><td>

<div class="wrap">

<div class="meta">
  <div><div class="k">Report / Accession</div><b>{{ rep.accession }}</b></div>
  <div><div class="k">Report date</div><b>{{ date }}</b></div>
  <div><div class="k">Report status</div><b>{{ rep.status }}</b></div>
  <div><div class="k">Test performed</div><b>{{ rep.test }}</b></div>
  <div><div class="k">Specimen / material</div><b>{{ rep.specimen }}</b></div>
  <div><div class="k">Reference genome</div><b>{{ rep.reference_genome }}</b></div>
  <div><div class="k">Reason for referral</div><b>{{ rep.referral_reason }}</b></div>
  <div><div class="k">Referring clinician</div><b>{{ rep.referring_clinician or "_______________________" }}</b></div>
  <div><div class="k">Family ID</div><b>{{ rep.family_id }}</b></div>
</div>

<h2 class="sec">Individuals analysed</h2>
<table><tr><th>Individual</th><th>Relationship</th><th>Sex</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Sequenced</th></tr>
{% for m in family %}
  <tr><td>{{ m.iid }}</td><td>{{ m.relationship }}</td><td>{{ m.sex }}</td><td>{% if m.status == 'Affected' %}<b>Affected</b>{% else %}{{ m.status }}{% endif %}</td><td{% if m.sequenced != 'Yes' %} class="muted"{% endif %}>{{ m.sequenced }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% for n in notes %}<div class="small muted">{{ n }}</div>{% endfor %}

{% if top %}
<h2 class="sec">Result — primary finding</h2>
{% set _cv = (top.clinvar or '')|lower %}
{% set _isP = ('pathogenic' in _cv and 'conflicting' not in _cv and 'benign' not in _cv) %}
{% set cls = 'P' if _isP else ('LP' if top.tier == 'A' else 'VUS') %}
{% set lbl = {'P':'PATHOGENIC','LP':'LIKELY PATHOGENIC (candidate)','VUS':'UNCERTAIN SIGNIFICANCE'}[cls] %}
<div class="result">
  <div class="lead">{{ top.gene }} &nbsp;{{ top.hgvsc }}{% if top.hgvsp and top.hgvsp != '.' %} ({{ top.hgvsp }}){% endif %} — {{ top.zygosity|replace('(affected)','')|trim }}
    <span class="badge {{ cls }}">{{ lbl }}</span></div>
  <div style="margin-top:5px">A rare, {{ top.consequence|replace('_',' ') }} in <b>{{ top.gene }}</b>, {{ top.zygosity }},
  segregating under a <b>{{ top.model|replace('_',' ') }}</b> model — consistent with <b>{{ rep.disease_name }}</b>.</div>
</div>
<div class="legend">Classification scale:
  <span class="chip B">Benign</span><span class="chip LB">Likely benign</span><span class="chip VUS">VUS</span><span class="chip LP">Likely pathogenic</span><span class="chip P">Pathogenic</span></div>

<h2 class="sec">Variant detail</h2>
<table>
 <tr><th style="width:26%">Field</th><th>Value</th></tr>
 <tr><td>Gene / transcript</td><td><b>{{ top.gene }}</b> · {{ top.hgvsc.split(':')[0] if ':' in top.hgvsc else top.hgvsc }}</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Variant (GRCh38)</td><td class="mono">{{ top.locus }}{% if top.rsid and top.rsid != '.' %} · {{ top.rsid }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
 <tr><td>cDNA / protein</td><td class="mono">{{ top.hgvsc }} &nbsp; {{ top.hgvsp }}</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Zygosity / consequence</td><td>{{ top.zygosity }} · {{ top.consequence|replace('_',' ') }}</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Inheritance</td><td>{{ top.inheritance_note }}</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Population frequency</td><td><b>{{ top.gnomad }}{% if top.gnomad_afr and top.gnomad_afr != '.' %} (AFR {{ top.gnomad_afr }}){% endif %}</b> (gnomAD)</td></tr>
{% if top.alphamissense and top.alphamissense != '.' %}
 <tr><td>In-silico (finalist)</td><td><b>AlphaMissense {{ top.alphamissense }}</b> · REVEL {{ top.revel }} · CADD {{ top.cadd }} · SIFT {{ top.sift }} · PolyPhen {{ top.polyphen }}</td></tr>
{% else %}
 <tr><td>In-silico</td><td>SIFT {{ top.sift }} · PolyPhen {{ top.polyphen }}{% if top.phylop and top.phylop != '.' %} · PhyloP {{ top.phylop }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endif %}
 <tr><td>Segregation</td><td>{{ top.segregation }}</td></tr>
 <tr><td>ClinVar</td><td>{% if top.clinvar and top.clinvar != '.' %}{{ top.clinvar }}{% else %}Not previously reported (novel){% endif %}</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Classification</td><td><b>{% if top.tier == 'A' %}Likely-pathogenic candidate{% else %}Variant of uncertain significance{% endif %}</b> — {{ top.tier_reason }}</td></tr>
</table>

<h2 class="sec">Interpretation</h2>
<p style="margin:3px 0">The finding above is consistent with <b>{{ rep.disease_name }}</b>: {{ top.gene }} matches the
clinical presentation, the variant is {{ top.gnomad }} in population databases, and it segregates with disease across
the sequenced relatives ({{ top.segregation }}).{% if rep.interpretation_extra %} {{ rep.interpretation_extra }}{% endif %}</p>

<h2 class="sec">Recommendations</h2>
<ul>
 <li><b>Orthogonal confirmation</b> of {{ top.gene }} {{ top.hgvsc.split(':')[-1] if ':' in top.hgvsc else top.hgvsc }} by <b>Sanger sequencing</b>{% if rep.confirm_note %} ({{ rep.confirm_note }}){% endif %}.</li>
 <li><b>Parental / segregation testing</b> — where a parent was not sequenced, test them to establish de-novo status and complete the segregation evidence.</li>
 <li><b>Functional validation</b> of the predicted effect to move from candidate toward a definitive classification.</li>
 <li><b>Clinical correlation</b> with the relevant phenotype/scoring for {{ rep.disease_name }}.</li>
{% if top_mgmt %} <li><b>Management (if confirmed)</b>: {{ top_mgmt }}</li>{% endif %}
 <li><b>Genetic counselling</b> regarding inheritance and recurrence risk.</li>
</ul>
{% else %}
<h2 class="sec">Result</h2>
<p>No variant met Tier A/B reporting criteria in the analysed panel under the applied models. See the technical appendix and full research report for details.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="sign">
  <div class="sig"><div class="small muted">Reviewed, interpreted and authorised by:</div>
    <div class="sigline"></div>
    <div class="role"><b>{{ lab.head_name }}</b><br><b>{{ lab.head_title }}</b><br>
      <span class="small muted">{{ lab.institute }}, {{ lab.university }}</span></div></div>
  <div class="sig" style="max-width:150px"><div class="small muted">Date</div><div class="sigline"></div>
    <div class="small muted">Signature / official stamp</div></div>
</div>
<div class="foot"><span><b>CONFIDENTIAL</b> — {{ lab.confidentiality|replace('CONFIDENTIAL — ','') }}</span><span>{{ rep.accession }}</span></div>

<div class="pagebreak"></div>
<h2 class="sec" style="margin-top:0">Supporting technical appendix</h2>

<h2 class="sec">Appendix A — Quality metrics</h2>
<table><tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th><th>Interpretation</th></tr>
{% for r in rep.qc_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r[0] }}</td><td>{{ r[1] }}</td><td>{{ r[2] }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
{% if not rep.qc_rows %}
{% for k,v in qc.sex.items() %}<tr><td>Sex — {{ k }}</td><td>declared {{ v.declared_sex }}, inferred {{ v.inferred_sex }} (chrX-het {{ v.x_het_rate }})</td><td>{{ 'concordant' if v.declared_sex==v.inferred_sex else 'CHECK' }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
{% for k,v in qc.pairwise.items() %}<tr><td>Relatedness — {{ k }}</td><td>concordance {{ v.concordance }} ({{ v.n_sites }} sites)</td><td></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
</table>

<h2 class="sec">Appendix B — Methods (summary)</h2>
<p class="small" style="margin:2px 0">Paired-end whole-exome sequencing aligned to {{ rep.reference_genome }} (bwa-mem2), duplicate-marked and
base-recalibrated (GATK BQSR). Per-sample QC gating preceded joint genotyping (GATK HaplotypeCaller → CombineGVCFs →
GenotypeGVCFs) with best-practice hard-filtering. Copy-number (CNVkit) and paralog/mapping quality were reviewed.
Variants were annotated with Ensembl VEP (consequence, MANE transcript, gnomAD frequencies, SIFT, PolyPhen); finalist
variants were re-scored with CADD, REVEL and AlphaMissense. Pedigree-aware Mendelian analysis, segregation,
monozygotic-twin concordance and ACMG-style tiering were performed against the {{ rep.panel_name }} gene panel.
Pipelines: CallForge (analysis) + FamilyForge (interpretation).</p>

<h2 class="sec">Limitations &amp; disclaimer</h2>
<ul class="small">
 <li>Where a parent was not sequenced, de-novo status and phase are inferred, not confirmed.</li>
 <li>Population frequencies and some in-silico metrics are bounded by the locally available databases; finalist scores were retrieved from authoritative external sources.</li>
 <li>This is a <b>research analysis</b>, not an accredited diagnostic result. Reported variants are candidates pending orthogonal confirmation, functional validation, and formal ACMG classification by an accredited laboratory before any clinical action.</li>
 <li>Whole-exome sequencing does not reliably detect deep-intronic, regulatory, repeat-expansion, balanced structural, or low-level mosaic variants; a negative or single finding does not exclude all genetic causes.</li>
</ul>
<div class="foot"><span><b>CONFIDENTIAL</b> · {{ lab.lab_name }} · {{ lab.institute }}, {{ lab.university }}</span><span>{{ rep.accession }}</span></div>

</div>
</td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</body></html>
